  "mutation_admission": {
    "status": "open",
    "gate": "LGSWF-094",
    "requires": [
      "SemanticRefresh@1 connects pre-execution and provisional-patch semantic refresh without becoming a second semantic truth authority",
      "before execution the supervisor verifies datasets views, capsule freshness, producer-bound source fallback, selected tests/proofs (including verified empty), and ContextPack against the attempt binding",
      "on provisional patch the surface scans changed symbols, calculates invalidation closure, updates noncanonical provisional obligations, rejects scope escapes fail-closed, and replans verification",
      "provisional roots remain attempt-bound and noncanonical and never publish as canonical datasets truth",
      "SemanticReconciliation@1 gates merge admission and refreshes canonical semantic state only after queue acceptance",
      "pre-merge gate verifies predicted effects, contracts, selected tests/proofs (including verified empty), governor disposition, assurance evidence, and seal identity against the candidate tree",
      "after queue acceptance the surface rescans the accepted canonical tree, compares predicted and observed deltas, invalidates dependents, updates the semantic snapshot, reevaluates goals, and revises until settled",
      "workers and accelerator surfaces never publish datasets canonical roots; only datasets authority publishes canonical roots",
      "predicted and observed semantic deltas must reconcile fail-closed; unmatched path or symbol deltas reject post-acceptance refresh",
      "every invalidation obligation propagates through provisional-patch and post-acceptance closures with related tests and proofs",
      "accepted tree root and semantic-state root identities remain exact across pre-merge seal, rescan, snapshot, and gate records",
      "MergeQueue require_pre_merge_semantic_gate and complete_with_semantic_reconciliation fail closed without an admitted gate",
      "acceptance requires independent fenced supervisor verification; worker completion or task status alone never authorizes acceptance",
      "binary floats are excluded from content-addressed refresh and reconciliation identities",
      "model proposals remain non-authoritative and never admit work"
    ],
    "prior_status": "Epic I open for dependency-ready work; Epic J unblocks fixed-point convergence"
  },
